---
import TrustPageLayout from '../layouts/TrustPageLayout.astro';
import { AMAZON_LABEL, MARKET_LABEL } from '../lib/site';
---

<TrustPageLayout
	title="Editorial Policy"
	description="How we evaluate pickleball products and keep recommendations independent."
	canonicalPath="/editorial-policy"
>
	<h2>What we cover</h2>
	<p>
		We focus on paddles, court shoes, and portable nets that {MARKET_LABEL} players actually search for and can buy via
		{AMAZON_LABEL}. Guides are written for beginners through advanced tournament players, including seniors and players
		with specific fit needs.
	</p>
	<h2>How we evaluate gear</h2>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Playing job:</strong> control, power, spin, comfort, portability, joint protection.</li>
		<li><strong>Catalog integrity:</strong> products referenced in articles must exist in our gear database.</li>
		<li><strong>Honesty about gaps:</strong> if a spec or claim isn’t confirmed, we mark it instead of inventing it.</li>
		<li><strong>Audience fit:</strong> a “best” pick is always best <em>for someone</em> — we say who.</li>
	</ul>
	<h2>Independence stance</h2>
	<p>
		Affiliate relationships do not dictate rankings. We do not accept payment for placements in editorial lists.
		Approximate catalog prices may appear for context; they are never presented as live Amazon prices. Always
		confirm current pricing and availability on {AMAZON_LABEL}.
	</p>
	<h2>Corrections</h2>
	<p>
		If something is wrong, email us via the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>. We update guides when products,
		rules context, or buying advice meaningfully change — and we display last-updated dates on articles.
	</p>
</TrustPageLayout>
